    "end": 645.768,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "So when you write a letter, there's always advice how to practice.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_63",
    "start": 646.749,
    "end": 652.99,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "And according to that student's kind of capability, capacity.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_64",
    "start": 653.51,
    "end": 666.652,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "So I think this, it doesn't really mention the name, but I think it was also written letter to somebody, I think who might have asked advice on the mind teaching, I think.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_65",
    "start": 667.692,
    "end": 695.116,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "like that so so of course mind teaching very important but I'm not talking from my experience but since I've been with Khyentse Rinpoche since very young age so I hear that Khyentse Rinpoche giving teaching I've seen how people practice and all that so personally no experience but I think of course mind teaching is the most important",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_66",
    "start": 696.863,
    "end": 708.451,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "Because I think the essence of all the Buddha's teachings is to, how do you say, subdue the mind.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_67",
    "start": 717.463,
    "end": 725.205,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "Since sometimes we say in Tibetan, something so close, something so near, that you won't see like your eyelashes.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_68",
    "start": 726.225,
    "end": 734.928,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "I don't know whether in the West you use this quote or not, but in Tibetan we say, because our eyelash is so close, so we don't really see that, see them.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_69",
    "start": 735.948,
    "end": 744.67,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "So you need a kind of, in order to really get the teaching of mind normally,",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_70",
    "start": 746.093,
    "end": 767.858,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "people will go through lots of practice, preliminary practice, ngondro practice, and from the ngondro, I think to become a really, to do a good practice or good practice, to become a good practitioner, I think that why we practice, I think that's very important.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_71",
    "start": 769.02,
    "end": 776.142,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "not just because it's fashionable, or not just because it sounds good, or not just as kind of temporary relaxing.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_72",
    "start": 777.003,
    "end": 788.427,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "The purpose why we want to practice Dharma has to, the reason why we want to practice has to be because of the, what we call the four changes of mind, or four thoughts.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_73",
    "start": 790.427,
    "end": 792.308,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "Four thoughts that turn the mind into Dharma.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_74",
    "start": 793.848,
    "end": 795.489,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "Then precious human life,",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_75",
    "start": 798.69,
    "end": 801.833,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "so much potential that we have.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_76",
    "start": 803.294,
    "end": 824.633,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "Then, of course, in the traditional classic teaching, there's all this reflection of not the, now we, in the traditional teaching that Tanjong Nyepakawa, the five things,",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_77",
    "start": 827.836,
    "end": 832.499,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "Anyway, 18, I don't know how to say it in English.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_78",
    "start": 835.74,
    "end": 842.464,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "So all these things to reflect, to see how precious human life is.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_79",
    "start": 842.484,
    "end": 850.168,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "So sometimes we can also use from the modern kind of thinking that if you look at the evolution of the",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_80",
    "start": 850.979,
    "end": 863.94,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "modern science, that how the human race started from being a cell, slowly to a fish, and then slowly, slowly to, you know, I'm sure more of you study in science.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_81",
    "start": 864.915,
    "end": 872.558,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "And then when I sometimes think, there are like millions of chance that we not become a human being, that we become a mushroom or we become a tree.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_82",
    "start": 875.299,
    "end": 881.242,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "So of course, mushroom and tree don't have the intelligence that we have.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_83",
    "start": 883.242,
    "end": 895.028,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "So I think from that evolution point of view, I think we can also look at how precious human life is because we have so much intelligence, so much potential.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_84",
    "start": 897.068,
    "end": 907.513,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "Then also people who have this precious human life, how many of us really utilize it properly?",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_85",
    "start": 911.772,
    "end": 915.713,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "Many people somehow take it for granted.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_86",
    "start": 916.833,
    "end": 930.458,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "There's a kind of a joke, one Tibetan Lama was teaching this precious human life to a Chinese student, and he said, oh, the precious human life is very rare, and the Chinese student said, the Lama, you've never been to China.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_87",
    "start": 937.183,
    "end": 938.604,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "So it's not like that, I think.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_88",
    "start": 938.905,
    "end": 943.949,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "Not just being a human, but someone who wants to give some meaning to one's life.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_89",
    "start": 945.13,
    "end": 945.631,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "Very rare.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_90",
    "start": 946.351,
    "end": 949.654,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "And those who want to give meaning to one's life, finding the right path.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_91",
    "start": 952.218,
    "end": 961.226,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "I think those things, by contemplating on those things, then we feel how precious human life is.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_92",
    "start": 961.286,
    "end": 962.246,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "So this is number one.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_93",
    "start": 962.667,
    "end": 972.535,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "And number two, I think what we call the impermanence, contemplating on impermanence, everything changes, nothing is permanent.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_94",
    "start": 974.438,
    "end": 983.896,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "And impermanence is not always bad news, because many people think impermanence is bad news, but impermanence is the natural of how things are.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_95",
    "start": 984.818,
    "end": 986.681,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "Rich become poor, poor become rich.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_96",
    "start": 988.1,
    "end": 991.602,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "lazy become diligent, diligent become lazy, everything changes.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_97",
    "start": 991.622,
    "end": 993.543,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "So that is how the things are.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_98",
    "start": 993.563,
    "end": 1005.009,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "So contemplating on impermanence, I think even in sutras and many teachings it says that one of the most important and especially for the people who wants to practice dharma.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_99",
    "start": 1006.39,
    "end": 1009.892,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "Then believing in understanding law of the cause and effect.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_100",
    "start": 1013.379,
    "end": 1016.481,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "Everything has a cause, everything has an effect.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_101",
    "start": 1016.521,
    "end": 1017.122,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "So believing.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_102",
    "start": 1017.202,
    "end": 1017.462,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "Trust.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_103",
    "start": 1017.822,
    "end": 1020.004,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "Then the suffering of the samsara.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_104",
    "start": 1020.284,
    "end": 1022.606,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "So all those things.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_105",
    "start": 1033.15,
    "end": 1045.457,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "I think the suffering of samsara we all gathered here, we have some sense of understanding of that, then we look for some kind of way to be out of the suffering of the samsara.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_106",
    "start": 1046.037,
    "end": 1056.783,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "So I think those four changes of mind, even though we heard this so many times, or even though it sounds quite kind of easy intellectually,",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_107",
    "start": 1057.867,
    "end": 1062.918,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "I think we really have to put into our heart and it has to come from our heart.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_108",
    "start": 1066.328,
    "end": 1082.752,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "Like this story in Batur Rinpoche, a story where when he was teaching the Four Thoughts to his student, and Batur Rinpoche is one of the great Tibetan, what's it called?",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_109",
    "start": 1082.852,
    "end": 1092.674,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "Yogi, master, who's like the best example of the practitioner who lived in Samanya Dzogchen Monastery.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_110",
    "start": 1093.895,
    "end": 1098.911,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "And Rinpoche would stay in the cave, and students would also stay in the cave.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_111",
    "start": 1100.307,
    "end": 1108.231,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "And then when there is no appointment or there is no timing, when the time is right, the master would come out and call for the student, hey, where you are?",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_112",
    "start": 1108.952,
    "end": 1113.755,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "And the student will come up from the bush or wherever he was meditating.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_113",
    "start": 1115.516,
    "end": 1122.039,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "If you've been to Tibet or you have seen the Tibetans, then you can imagine, especially in Shechen area.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_114",
    "start": 1122.059,
    "end": 1124.621,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "It's a big cloud like that coming out.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_115",
    "start": 1125.621,
    "end": 1126.902,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "And they would sit on the rock.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_116",
    "start": 1128.897,
    "end": 1133.14,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "And Bhadur Rinpoche would say one sentence.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_117",
    "start": 1136.322,
    "end": 1138.663,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "Precious human life is very rare.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_118",
    "start": 1140.684,
    "end": 1144.867,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "And then teacher would cry, and the student would cry.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_119",
    "start": 1145.687,
    "end": 1148.029,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "So then they cry, cry, cry, the teaching finish.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_120",
    "start": 1153.492,
    "end": 1157.835,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "So then next day again, the lama calls and student comes, so like that.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_121",
    "start": 1158.708,
    "end": 1161.149,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "So sometimes we don't need too much blah blah blah talking.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_122",
    "start": 1162.21,
    "end": 1166.892,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "I think the main thing, I think it has to come really from the heart.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_123",
    "start": 1168.573,
    "end": 1168.933,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "Like that.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_124",
    "start": 1170.254,
    "end": 1172.055,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "So these things I think are very important.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
